# C-10k self-test: per-pair verdicts and cut arcs.
# Graph as toycert (1->2->3->1, 3->4; shortest 1->4 = 180, 1->3 = 150) plus a short
# cut 1->4 of 5 ps (a fast-fall tap, say).  Data A (node 1) latest 170, data B (node 2)
# latest 100.
# expected:
#   pair-pass   pairs (A,4) +10 and (B,3) +50: PASS +10 (the cross product would fail: A vs 3 = -20)
#   cross-fail  same instance as a cross product (targets 3 and 4): FAIL -20
#   pair-fail   pair (A,3): FAIL -20
#   nocut-lie   without `cut 1 4` the potential 180 at pin 4 is refuted by the 5 ps arc: CERTBAD
graph 5
g 1 2 0 100 200 100 200 100 200 100 200 100 200 100 200
g 2 3 0 50 60 50 60 50 60 50 60 50 60 50 60
g 3 1 0 10 20 10 20 10 20 10 20 10 20 10 20
g 3 4 0 30 40 30 40 30 40 30 40 30 40 30 40
g 1 4 1 5 9 5 9 5 9 5 9 5 9 5 9
inst pair-pass
setup 0
data 1 2
arc 0 1 50 170
arc 0 2 10 100
late 0 1 0 0 0 0
cut 1 4
pair 1 4 0
pair 2 3 0
cap 180
pot 2 0 100 3 0 150
end
inst cross-fail
setup 0
data 1 2
arc 0 1 50 170
arc 0 2 10 100
late 0 1 0 0 0 0
cut 1 4
target 4 0
target 3 0
cap 180
pot 2 0 100 3 0 150
end
inst pair-fail
setup 0
data 1
arc 0 1 50 170
late 0 1 0 0 0 0
cut 1 4
pair 1 3 0
cap 180
pot 2 0 100 3 0 150
end
inst nocut-lie
setup 0
data 1
arc 0 1 50 170
late 0 1 0 0 0 0
pair 1 4 0
cap 180
pot 2 0 100 3 0 150
end
